text:
TITS love was like the red, red rose;
She walked in beauty like the night;


Hers was the iily's swee. repose;
She was vision Of delight
No sweeter flower ever grew;


She was nympt, woodland fay;
Their partings always made h;rl blue,
And SO he married her one day.
The swift years whirled in dizzy fight;
His love grew cranky, stern and thin.
She walked in beauty like the night,
Armed with maple rolling pin.
Such is the fate OF many sport


From humble clerk to pompous earl,
Who lets the poets help him coiirt


And steals their lines to tell his girl.

